herolte: the scenario bench, heroscen=<settle s> with herogov=2 (0468, D-0113)

min98-min101: every comparison cost a BOOT write, a manual run of gestures and gave one sample per condition. The kernel now plays the same gestures every time through sweet_hid_touch (the real touch driver's entry point, stamping herolte_touch_last_mach so the governor sees a finger) and measures each run: paging (10 swipes), spotlight (3 pull-downs), 15 s idle. One boot runs three caps of the big cluster (2288, 1976, 1664 MHz) as A-B-C then C-B-A, so drift (temperature, battery, time since boot) cancels. After each run one line: duration, mean battery current while discharging and its sample count, frames presented, their spacing in ms buckets (<20 <40 <70 <120 <250 >=250: the fluidity measure the fps lines never gave, E-0317), temperature, clock changes, governor samples saturated at the cap. Needs: governor g2_cap and statistics exported, frame spacing histogram in SweetFramebuffer.cpp, current accumulator in herolte_battery.c. heroscen only.

